analysisWe need to write an assert statement reflecting the comment:

"// @@@ If the bit index is non-negative, then for each index i between 0 and the length of the bit set (exclusive), except for the bit at bitIndex, the value of the bit remains unchanged."

We are inside method flip(int bitIndex). The comment says: If the bit index is non-negative, then for each index i between 0 and the length of the bit set (exclusive), except for the bit at bitIndex, the value of the bit remains unchanged.

We need to express that after flip, for all i where 0 <= i < this.length() and i != bitIndex, this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)). Also precondition: bitIndex >= 0.

Thus assert: bitIndex >= 0 => (\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.length() && i != bitIndex; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)));

But note that length() may change after flip? Flipping could set a new highest set bit, increasing length. The comment says "between 0 and the length of the bit set (exclusive)". Which length? Probably after the operation? Usually length() after flip could be larger if we set a bit beyond previous length. But they say "except for the bit at bitIndex". So for other bits within range, unchanged. So we can use this.length() after operation. So assert: bitIndex >= 0 => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.length() && i != bitIndex; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));

We need to use \old on length? Not needed; we compare bits. Might also need to ensure i < this.length() after. That's fine.

Thus final assert:

assert bitIndex >= 0 => (\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.length() && i != bitIndex; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)));

Make sure parentheses correct: bitIndex >= 0 => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.length() && i != bitIndex; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));

But need parentheses around the \forall expression as right side of =>. In examples they used parentheses: bitIndex>=0 && index<=9 => \forall ... . For implication they used parentheses only when needed. Here we have implication with right side being a quantified expression. So we can write:

assert bitIndex >= 0 => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.length() && i != bitIndex; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));

