analysisWe need to produce an assert statement reflecting the comment.

Comment: 
// @@@ If the bit index is non-negative, then for each index i between 0 and the length of the bit set (exclusive), except for the bit at bitIndex, the value of the bit remains unchanged.

Method flip(int bitIndex). Preconditions: bitIndex >=0 (since if negative throws). After flip, bits other than bitIndex remain same.

We need to refer to length of bit set. There's method length() which returns logical size (index of highest set bit +1). So "the length of the bit set (exclusive)" is this.length(). So for each i where 0 <= i < this.length() && i != bitIndex, the value after operation equals old value.

We can write: assert bitIndex >= 0 => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.length() && i != bitIndex; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));

But need to use \old for old value. Also need to use \result? No return.

So final assert: assert bitIndex >= 0 => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.length() && i != bitIndex; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));

